# Keeping these out is not only about image size.
#
# `.env` and `infra/*.tfvars` hold real credentials, and a COPY that sweeps
# them in bakes them into a layer that survives every later deletion. An image
# is distributed; a layer is not private because the file was removed in the
# next step.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
infra
*.tfvars
*.tfstate*

node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/test

docs
*.md
!README.md

# Workspace members the image does not run.
#
# Their manifests are NOT excluded: pnpm resolves workspace links at install
# time and fails on a missing member, so `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# needs every package.json even for packages whose source never ships.
# Excluding the directory outright is what breaks the build — the first
# version of this file did exactly that.
apps/web/*
!apps/web/package.json
apps/mobile/*
!apps/mobile/package.json
tools/loadtest/*
!tools/loadtest/package.json
tools/devdata/*
!tools/devdata/package.json
